    {
      "caption": "Sex-linked inheritance",
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "id": "s4",
      "narration": "Haemophilia rides on the X chromosome. Cross a carrier mother with a normal father: half her sons inherit the faulty allele — and with no second X to mask it, they show the trait — while half her daughters become carriers.",
